{"kind":"ResearchObservationCreated","event_id":"event_aa6e88796ce64df79a8ae589d9b79a35","document_ref":"htr:research","correlation_id":"experiment_run_20e3ae81c4b04d2fa2cda956c3415b62","causation_id":"event_7970260535e94d55a6a0aafff12dd2a5","schema_version":1,"recorded_at":"2026-07-30T18:24:44.386470+00:00","reconciliation_policy_version":null,"capability_matrix_version":null,"confidence_policy_version":null,"feedback_policy_version":null,"alignment_algorithm_version":null,"project_id":null,"dataset_id":"dataset_340076dbf11e43d69eb27ca95c31fb44","dataset_version_id":"dataset_version_17646156c9eb40df9922769b9f534306","experiment_id":"experiment_a6b6e77dd7a0431eb2f23391f53af49d","experiment_version_id":"experiment_version_784214ca1c954857bc494771d977a89b","experiment_run_id":"experiment_run_20e3ae81c4b04d2fa2cda956c3415b62","method_run_id":null,"subject_id":"research_observation_b359224960cf49219c2de4541dd714b3","actor_type":"system","actor_id":"scripts/run_satrn_repetition_diagnostic.py","source_component":"htr.persistence.durable_store","application_commit":null,"observation_ref":"research_observation_b359224960cf49219c2de4541dd714b3","summary":"SATRN@a40c7093 returned the identical string 'staden den 27 dennes' for 6 of 15 byte-distinct line crops; not an integration defect","evidence_refs":["docs/experiments/technical-reliability-screening/diagnostic/satrn_repetition_diagnostic.json","docs/experiments/technical-reliability-screening/satrn-repetition-diagnostic.md","docs/experiments/technical-reliability-screening/smoke-test/smoke_test_results.json","src/archivetrust/providers/satrn/README.md","input_crop_1d9a3a4f709a4472ac488189f154b5c4","input_crop_50dc8a1c4cbb493c9af29979b467f7dc","input_crop_377f189a2c5f491b81ec4964709a5a40","input_crop_1af212a49c2145b98c36a2cd7f98049e","input_crop_c1c74279326c4fa89c030fa55bb592af","input_crop_fb0310f8ad5a481da6e2f9e2a19ac9ad","input_crop_4f034275f85f42d8bdbf6659998939f7","input_crop_0a37475cf52942bba20b31918530feea","input_crop_0c89a9e029fb443eb4c368b47ece51f8","input_crop_2aab3b7726bc4fa5a1531687ace3f10a","input_crop_9dc3a7f35d71438391d8f93c32efc49e"],"observation":{"observation_id":"research_observation_b359224960cf49219c2de4541dd714b3","observation_type":"model_limitation","title":"SATRN@a40c7093 returned the identical string 'staden den 27 dennes' for 6 of 15 byte-distinct line crops; not an integration defect","description":"On 15 real line crops cut from 5 real pages of the Swedish witchcraft-trial court-record corpus, SATRN at revision a40c7093232eaa47a83ce6469fc4abd033486bdc returned the identical string 'staden den 27 dennes' for 6 crops (input_crop_1d9a3a4f709a4472ac488189f154b5c4, input_crop_50dc8a1c4cbb493c9af29979b467f7dc, input_crop_377f189a2c5f491b81ec4964709a5a40, input_crop_1af212a49c2145b98c36a2cd7f98049e, input_crop_c1c74279326c4fa89c030fa55bb592af, input_crop_fb0310f8ad5a481da6e2f9e2a19ac9ad) and 'talan att' for 4 more (input_crop_c2253d155b8a4ae8acaccdb7587a2574, input_crop_91595c063b0b4842b8f61d664d71f99c, input_crop_368077e5975c47bc9e4c1661442eab93, input_crop_5ea401d261f345de8ec874e634e925f6): 7 distinct outputs over 15 distinct inputs (ratio 0.4667). Florence-2, reading the byte-identical crops, produced 15 distinct outputs (ratio 1.0). The 15 crops are genuinely different images: all 15 PNG-byte SHA-256 digests are distinct, all 15 decoded-pixel SHA-256 digests are distinct, none is blank (per-crop grayscale standard deviation 29.8-84.3 over 227-256 distinct levels), and each file's size matches the byte_size the smoke test recorded. The integration-defect hypotheses were tested and excluded. Every adapter invocation received its own fresh child process (15 distinct PIDs for 15 calls); the worker argv carried the source crop path itself, so no temporary file is created and none can be reused or collide; each crop's bytes were unchanged by its own call and matched the manifest hash; the worker reported the same pinned model and config revision on every call. Most decisively, pass E reproduced the identical 7/15 constancy -- and every confidence value to full float precision -- through mmocr.apis.TextRecInferencer called directly inside .venv-satrn in ONE process with ONE model load, bypassing SatrnAdapter, facade.py and _worker.py entirely. The 6 identical strings carry 6 different confidence scores (0.5366043906658888, 0.536318052560091, 0.5346601057797671, 0.5660757340490818, 0.5236199896782636, 0.5265959832817316); a cached, stale or cross-wired result would have carried an identical score too. All 5 passes (same order, reversed order, isolated processes, and the reference API) returned byte-identical text and bit-identical confidence for every crop, so the behaviour is fully deterministic and order-independent. The committed baseline run independently recorded this same checkpoint returning 'till den 23 Januarii' for a line whose reference text is 'bekiendt. Säger och deth hon Minnes hoon Tuå gånger waritt' -- a short, generic, date-shaped phrase with no lexical overlap with the line, produced on a different image by a different pipeline with no repetition question in play (see htr/knowledge/baseline_knowledge.py, SATRN_OUTPUT_TEXT). Recorded for these 15 crops and this configuration only. This observation asserts nothing about SATRN's suitability for the full corpus: that is an operational decision requiring the ScreeningPolicy/ScreeningDecision entities design-audit.md §3.3 records as not yet existing, and SATRN remains in scope for the forthcoming benchmark. The crops both methods read were detected by a Florence-2-family line detector, so one screened method's own model family controlled the input the other was judged on. Flagged at Checkpoint 1, not neutralized here, and restated because this observation quotes a SATRN-vs-Florence-2 contrast.","scope":{"experiment_id":"experiment_a6b6e77dd7a0431eb2f23391f53af49d","experiment_version_id":"experiment_version_784214ca1c954857bc494771d977a89b","experiment_run_ids":["experiment_run_20e3ae81c4b04d2fa2cda956c3415b62"],"unit_of_analysis":"line_crop","covered_unit_ids":["input_crop_1d9a3a4f709a4472ac488189f154b5c4","input_crop_50dc8a1c4cbb493c9af29979b467f7dc","input_crop_377f189a2c5f491b81ec4964709a5a40","input_crop_4f034275f85f42d8bdbf6659998939f7","input_crop_0a37475cf52942bba20b31918530feea","input_crop_1af212a49c2145b98c36a2cd7f98049e","input_crop_0c89a9e029fb443eb4c368b47ece51f8","input_crop_2aab3b7726bc4fa5a1531687ace3f10a","input_crop_9dc3a7f35d71438391d8f93c32efc49e","input_crop_c1c74279326c4fa89c030fa55bb592af","input_crop_c2253d155b8a4ae8acaccdb7587a2574","input_crop_91595c063b0b4842b8f61d664d71f99c","input_crop_368077e5975c47bc9e4c1661442eab93","input_crop_5ea401d261f345de8ec874e634e925f6","input_crop_fb0310f8ad5a481da6e2f9e2a19ac9ad"],"dataset_id":"dataset_340076dbf11e43d69eb27ca95c31fb44","dataset_version_id":"dataset_version_17646156c9eb40df9922769b9f534306","method_ids":["satrn","florence2"],"model_version_ids":["a40c7093232eaa47a83ce6469fc4abd033486bdc","nazounoryuu/florence_base__mixed__line_bbox__ocr@994f47e8a0e8d77cb2e11528665efd07a855c3af"],"method_run_ids":[],"normalization_profile":null,"ground_truth_ref":null,"configuration_ref":"device=auto/cuda; Resize(scale=(400, 64), keep_ratio=False); mean=(123.675, 116.28, 103.53); std=(58.395, 57.12, 57.375); segmentation=nazounoryuu/florence_base__mixed__page__line_od"},"supporting_evidence":[{"kind":"external_document","reference_id":"docs/experiments/technical-reliability-screening/diagnostic/satrn_repetition_diagnostic.json","stream":null,"note":"machine-readable diagnostic: crop manifest, all 5 passes, integration checks"},{"kind":"external_document","reference_id":"docs/experiments/technical-reliability-screening/satrn-repetition-diagnostic.md","stream":null,"note":"the written diagnostic report"},{"kind":"external_document","reference_id":"docs/experiments/technical-reliability-screening/smoke-test/smoke_test_results.json","stream":null,"note":"Checkpoint 3 smoke test: satrn_output_constancy = 7/15, florence2 = 15/15"},{"kind":"external_document","reference_id":"src/archivetrust/providers/satrn/README.md","stream":null,"note":"documented checkpoint, isolated-venv setup and prior measured inference behaviour"},{"kind":"input_crop","reference_id":"input_crop_1d9a3a4f709a4472ac488189f154b5c4","stream":"docs/experiments/technical-reliability-screening/smoke-test/smoke_test_events.jsonl","note":"returned 'staden den 27 dennes' at confidence 0.5366043906658888"},{"kind":"input_crop","reference_id":"input_crop_50dc8a1c4cbb493c9af29979b467f7dc","stream":"docs/experiments/technical-reliability-screening/smoke-test/smoke_test_events.jsonl","note":"returned 'staden den 27 dennes' at confidence 0.536318052560091"},{"kind":"input_crop","reference_id":"input_crop_377f189a2c5f491b81ec4964709a5a40","stream":"docs/experiments/technical-reliability-screening/smoke-test/smoke_test_events.jsonl","note":"returned 'staden den 27 dennes' at confidence 0.5346601057797671"},{"kind":"input_crop","reference_id":"input_crop_1af212a49c2145b98c36a2cd7f98049e","stream":"docs/experiments/technical-reliability-screening/smoke-test/smoke_test_events.jsonl","note":"returned 'staden den 27 dennes' at confidence 0.5660757340490818"},{"kind":"input_crop","reference_id":"input_crop_c1c74279326c4fa89c030fa55bb592af","stream":"docs/experiments/technical-reliability-screening/smoke-test/smoke_test_events.jsonl","note":"returned 'staden den 27 dennes' at confidence 0.5236199896782636"},{"kind":"input_crop","reference_id":"input_crop_fb0310f8ad5a481da6e2f9e2a19ac9ad","stream":"docs/experiments/technical-reliability-screening/smoke-test/smoke_test_events.jsonl","note":"returned 'staden den 27 dennes' at confidence 0.5265959832817316"},{"kind":"input_crop","reference_id":"input_crop_4f034275f85f42d8bdbf6659998939f7","stream":"docs/experiments/technical-reliability-screening/smoke-test/smoke_test_events.jsonl","note":"distinct-output control crop"},{"kind":"input_crop",